{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three pumpkins are weighed two at a time in all possible ways. The weights of the pairs of pumpkins are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kg, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kg and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kg. How much does the lightest pumpkin weigh?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3dbaeaeddc98fee2944ebf5195224590fc94fcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 6 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 8 \\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"529\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the weights of the lightest pumpkin, second lightest pumpkin, and heaviest pumpkin, respectively. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d71af8385dc0d359d7b2f01544977591615ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f64fa09adde6ea5c982b9040292fb845c6b880d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + z = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b6d96cb8866b06d8cb95e44b2aa14a2c008b6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + z = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From the third equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab0733d17915d4246cd18207542e89e11fc13e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 15 - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, so we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be4a6678f4916c8f908b145cfac0f07834eb10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 15 - y = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/7735c0186efa30b1b1729e3eb6cbe04405c250b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - y = 13 - 15 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />. Adding this to the first equation, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/25065264fbfa7347a96f7a44c79c8c5099f9f40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + x - y = 12 - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c93df85865af3c2ebedba00c65cd2725b0ab28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ac3f26ac91d7a4a3756efe16c839b34af74ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{10}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 5 \\text{ km}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same variables as solution 1, and get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d71af8385dc0d359d7b2f01544977591615ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f64fa09adde6ea5c982b9040292fb845c6b880d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + z = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b6d96cb8866b06d8cb95e44b2aa14a2c008b6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + z = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Adding the first two equations together, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/7940ea3ad3376772276b5dc6cf7aa3e86a9d3eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + x + z = 12 + 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/2495c5aa32dd71a48eec762703b7b713d6ed9c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + y + z = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b6d96cb8866b06d8cb95e44b2aa14a2c008b6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + z = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> into this, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0066c298639573e4bdb0049e837ccf5b557471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 15 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83bc7279593b1347c6851a21579e764bb42ebb12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 25 - 15 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ac3f26ac91d7a4a3756efe16c839b34af74ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{10}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 5 \\text{ km}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;b